t_contract=2, verdict, disposition, reason all pre…\n      asserts: # SPEC-10 [#1846/SPEC-10]: every terminal exit path writes v2 envelope\nNEGCTL PASS SPEC-11\n      design : plugin.sh derives output path from ZBUILD_ARTIFACT_DIR; no state_file-derived path\n      asserts: assert_fail \"[#1846/SPEC-11] plugin.sh must not derive output path from state_file/state_dir\" \\\nNEGCTL PASS SPEC-12\n      design : pr_url and gate_aggregator_result resolved via ZBUILD_STAGE_INPUTS; plugin.sh constructs no pr-url.t…\n      asserts: assert_fail \"[#1846/SPEC-12] plugin.sh must not hardcode pr-url.txt or gate-aggregator-result.json p…\nNEGCTL PASS SPEC-13\n      design : all error exit paths return rc=1; no exit path returns rc=2 or higher\n      asserts: assert_pass \"[#1846/SPEC-13] plugin.sh has no non-comment exit/return with rc>=2\"\nNEGCTL PASS SPEC-14\n      design : all three valid verdicts (deployed, error, skipped) are exercised with v2-shaped result in tests\n      asserts: assert_eq \"[#1846/SPEC-14] successful deploy writes verdict=deployed (v2)\" \"deployed\" \"$_vs\"\nNEGCTL PASS SPEC-15 guard_spec\n      design : manifest has no config.router block; manifest_router_knob returns empty for timeout_s and max_turns\n      asserts: assert_eq \"[#1846/SPEC-15] manifest_router_knob timeout_s returns empty (no config.router)\" \\\nNEGCTL PASS SPEC-16 guard_spec\n      design : manifest outputs.deploy_result retains primary: true\n      asserts: assert_pass \"[#1846/SPEC-16] manifest outputs.deploy_result declares primary: true\"\nNEGCTL PASS SPEC-17 guard_spec\n      design : manifest provides.role = deploy_agent; provides.events = exactly the four declared events\n      asserts: assert_pass \"[#1846/SPEC-17] manifest provides.role = deploy_agent\"\nNEGCTL PASS SPEC-18 guard_spec\n      design : manifest hooks block declares only run: deploy_agent_run; no cleanup: entry\n      asserts: assert_pass \"[#1846/SPEC-18] manifest hooks block declares run: deploy_agent_run\"\nNEGCTL PASS SPEC-19\n      design : dry-run deploy-result.json carries verdict=deployed, disposition=complete, reason present (full v2 e…\n      asserts: assert_eq \"[#1846/SPEC-19] dry-run carries verdict=deployed\" \"deployed\" \"$_dry_v\"\nNEGCTL PASS SPEC-20\n      design : deploy-release returns non-zero → deploy-result.json disposition=unavailable\n      asserts: assert_eq \"[#1846/SPEC-20] deploy-release non-zero → disposition=unavailable\" \\\nNEGCTL PASS SPEC-21\n      design : deploy-release plugin file absent → deploy-result.json disposition=broken\n      asserts: assert_eq \"[#1846/SPEC-21] deploy-release absent → disposition=broken\" \\\nNEGCTL PASS SPEC-22 guard_spec\n      design : manifest config.valid_verdicts lists exactly the three emittable verdicts: deployed, error, skipped\n      asserts: assert_pass \"[#1846/SPEC-22] manifest config.valid_verdicts includes $_vv\"\nNEGCTL PASS SPEC-23\n      design : with ZBUILD_ARTIFACT_DIR set to a non-default path before deploy_agent_run, the result is written to…\n      asserts: assert_eq \"[#1846/SPEC-23] deploy_agent_run exits 0 in dry-run with non-default ZBUILD_ARTIFACT_DIR …\nNEGCTL PASS SPEC-24\n      design : manifest carries router-budget-absence comment documenting that deploy makes no LLM calls (strings \"…\n      asserts: assert_pass \"[#1846/SPEC-24] manifest carries 'router budgets: none' comment\"\nREACHABILITY PASS plugins/agent/deploy/manifest.yaml\n### secret-scan (verdict: pass)\n## secret-scan — pass\n\n- clean diff — no secrets found\n### assertion-integrity (verdict: pass)\n## assertion-integrity — pass\n\n- declared acceptance testfiles are unchanged since authoring\n\n- files checked against the authored digests\n- violations: none\n### issue-acceptance (verdict: pass)\n## issue-acceptance — pass\n\n- Every issue requirement is met — v2 envelope on all exit paths, rc ∈ {0,1}, name-matched inputs via ZBUILD_STAGE_INPUTS, no hardcoded artifact paths, valid_verdicts declared, primary:true retained, provides.role/events declared, cleanup hook absent and SPEC-18 verifies it, router-budget absence documented; all 24 SPECs pass and the test suite is green.\n\n- every requirement the issue states is met by the change\n### gate-aggregator (verdict: pass)\n## gate-aggregator — pass\n\n- rolled up 6 gate(s) into verdict pass\n\n- failed: none\n- fault: none declared",
  "output": "{\n  \"score\": 4,\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"plugins/agent/deploy/plugin.sh\",\n      \"category\": \"logic\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"line\": 163,\n      \"message\": \"The new code calls `deploy_release_run` with no arguments; the deploy-release plugin (`plugins/tool/deploy-release/plugin.sh` lines 22-35) treats a missing `state_file` arg as a hard error, writes `verdict=error/disposition=broken` to ZBUILD_ARTIFACT_DIR, and returns 1 — which the deploy plugin catches and overwrites with `disposition=unavailable` — making every real (non-dry-run) production deploy permanently fail at this call site.\",\n      \"introduced\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"plugins/tool/deploy-release/plugin.sh\",\n      \"category\": \"logic\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"line\": 37,\n      \"message\": \"deploy-release derives its own `artifacts_dir` from `dirname \\\"$state_file\\\"` (line 37-38), so even if the calling convention were fixed to pass a dummy state_file, the artifacts_dir used by deploy-release would diverge from `ZBUILD_ARTIFACT_DIR` used by the deploy plugin, meaning the two plugins would write to different paths and the deploy plugin's success-path result could silently miss the release artefacts.\",\n      \"introduced\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"plugins/agent/deploy/plugin.sh\",\n      \"category\": \"logic\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"line\": 44,\n      \"message\": \"When ZBUILD_ARTIFACT_DIR is unset, `deploy_agent_run` returns 1 immediately without writing any result file; the engine receives a missing result rather than a structured `verdict=error` envelope, which may route through a different (potentially unguarded) engine failure path than the one the v2 contract expects.\",\n      \"introduced\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"plugins/agent/deploy/plugin.sh\",\n      \"category\": \"coverage\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"line\": 168,\n      \"message\": \"Tests mock `deploy_release_run` via `_ZBUILD_DEPLOY_RELEASE_LOADED=1` for every run-path test (SPEC-2, SPEC-14, SPEC-20), so the actual interface between deploy and deploy-release is never exercised; the test suite gives a green result for a production-breaking interface mismatch because the mock returns 0 unconditionally rather than validating the call signature.\",\n      \"introduced\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"plugins/agent/deploy/plugin.sh\",\n      \"category\": \"logic\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"line\": 41,\n      \"message\": \"`_deploy_write_result` pipes `jq -n ...` into `atomic_write` without a `# sigpipe-ok` annotation; the CLAUDE.md SIGPIPE rule prohibits unannotated pipes in `plugins/` — if `atomic_write` exits early for any reason (e.g. ENOSPC), jq receives SIGPIPE and exits non-zero, causing `_deploy_write_result` to return non-zero under `set -euo pipefail` without having written the result file, leaving the engine with no artifact.\",\n      \"introduced\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"plugins/agent/deploy/tests/deploy-test.sh\",\n      \"category\": \"coverage\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"line\": 64,\n      \"message\": \"`_make_state` exports `ZBUILD_STAGE_INPUTS` and `ZBUILD_ARTIFACT_DIR` into the calling shell (by design), so every test that runs after a `_make_state` call inherits those paths; a future test inserted between two existing tests without its own `_make_state` call will silently use the previous test's artifact directory and produce false-green assertions.\",\n      \"introduced\": true\n    }\n  ]\n}",
